arbohydrates.\n\n5. **Estimation for Sweets and Snacks:**  \n   - For branded or common sweets/snacks (e.g., gumdrops, granola bar, popsicle), use nutrition data for the average item by weight or per piece as appropriate.\n\n6. **Beverages:**  \n   - For sodas, juices, or other drinks, assume the standard, most common formulation unless otherwise specified (e.g., regular cola, 100% juice).\n\n7. **Carbohydrate Calculation:**  \n   - Sum the carbohydrate values for all components, using the actual portion sizes consumed.\n\n8. **If Estimation Is Not Possible:**  \n   - If a food cannot be matched to a standard or typical item, or if key details are missing, return {\"total_carbohydrates\": -1}.\n\n9. **Output Format:**  \n   - Return a dictionary: {\"total_carbohydrates\": total_carbohydrate_grams}  \n   - The value should be a number only (no units or extra text).\n\n**Example 1:**  \nText: \"For breakfast, I enjoyed 248 grams of cocoa mix reconstituted with water, along with a 55-gram boiled egg and 301 grams of cooked steel cut oats.\"  \nResponse: {\"total_carbohydrates\": 66.39}\n\n**Example 2:**  \nText: \"Snacking on a Popsicle, a cup of gumdrops, and one Quaker Chewy Granola Bar.\"  \nResponse: {\"total_carbohydrates\": 244.05}\n\n**Example 3:**  \nText: \"I enjoyed a 15g serving of coconut sambal alongside 43g of fish curry and 224g of string hopper for dinner, plus 325g of water.\"  \nResponse: {\"total_carbohydrates\": 179.33}\n\n**Example 4:**  \nText: \"For lunch, I'm having a 512g cola and a 340g burrito filled with meat, beans, rice, and sour cream.\"  \nResponse: {\"total_carbohydrates\": 107.10}\n\n---\n\n# Prediction\nQuery: {{ text }}\nAnswer:",
