tes\": total_carbohydrate_grams}\n   - Output only the numeric value (no units).\n   - If you cannot make a reasonable estimate, return {\"total_carbohydrates\": -1}.\n\n**Examples:**\n\nText: \"I consumed 200g cooked white rice and a 355ml can of regular cola.\"  \nResponse: {\"total_carbohydrates\": 100.8}\n\nText: \"Breakfast includes a large round cornbread muffin and a bottle of diet root beer.\"  \nResponse: {\"total_carbohydrates\": 78.54}\n\nText: \"For dinner, I'm having a 254g burrito filled with meat and sour cream along with a 360g diet cola.\"  \nResponse: {\"total_carbohydrates\": 34.19}\n\nText: \"I drank 250g of syrup water (syrup diluted with water, typical preparation).\"  \nResponse: {\"total_carbohydrates\": [estimate based on diluted syrup water per 250g]}\n\nText: \"For breakfast, I enjoyed 248 grams of cocoa mix reconstituted with water, along with a 55-gram boiled egg and 301 grams of cooked steel cut oats.\"  \nResponse: {\"total_carbohydrates\": 66.39}\n\nText: \"Snacking on a Popsicle, a cup of gumdrops, and one Quaker Chewy Granola Bar.\"  \nResponse: {\"total_carbohydrates\": 244.05}\n\nText: \"I enjoyed a 15g serving of coconut sambal alongside 43g of fish curry and 224g of string hopper for dinner, plus 325g of water.\"  \nResponse: {\"total_carbohydrates\": 179.33}\n\nText: \"For my snack, I have 3.4g of coconut oil, 10g of eggplant that's been broiled, and 0.8g of onion. I\u2019m also including 20g of cooked pig intestines, 150g of steamed white rice, and 3.3g of raw tomato.\"  \nResponse: {\"total_carbohydrates\": 47.44}\n\n**Key Reminders:**  \n- Always use the carbohydrate value for the food as actually consumed (prepared, cooked, reconstituted, or raw).\n- Do not use the dry mix value for reconstituted items\u2014use the value for the prepared drink/food.\n- For composite items, candies, or branded goods, sum all relevant carbohydrate sources by standard or branded nutrition facts.\n\n# Prediction\nQuery: {{ text }}\nAnswer:"
